---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj27.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Japan's Layered National and Local Tax System" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Corporation Tax, Inhabitant Tax, and Enterprise Tax" },
        { id: "s4", label: "THE KEY NUANCE — the Size-Based Portion of Enterprise Tax" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Recognition Timing for Current Tax Expense" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Classifying Enterprise Tax Between Income-Based and Size-Based Portions" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Worked Example — Total Current Tax Expense" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="hub">
      <div class="hub-box">
        <div class="hub-title">ASBJ Statement No. 27 — Accounting Standard for Current Income Taxes</div>
        <div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Japan GAAP (J-GAAP) · 法人税、住民税及び事業税等に関する会計基準 · Recently revised (2026) — verify against current ASBJ materials · JPY examples</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout info callout--centered">RECENCY NOTE: ASBJ has recently (2026) issued a revision to this Statement. The core historical framework described below is well-established, but the precise substance of the most recent revision should be verified against ASBJ's current published materials.</div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Recognising the current period's tax liability across multiple layered taxes</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 27 governs the RECOGNITION of "CURRENT" income tax expense — the amount of tax PAYABLE (or refundable) for the CURRENT period, based on TAXABLE profit — DISTINCT from the DEFERRED tax accounting addressed by ASBJ Statement No. 28. A DISTINCTIVE feature of Japan's system is that "income taxes," in the ACCOUNTING sense, actually comprise SEVERAL separate, layered NATIONAL and LOCAL taxes.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Japan's Layered National and Local Tax System</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">All companies subject to Japan's corporate tax regime</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies subject to Japan's CORPORATE tax system, which — DISTINCTIVELY — layers NATIONAL corporation tax TOGETHER with LOCAL inhabitant tax and enterprise tax, EACH governed by its OWN tax rules but TOGETHER treated as "income taxes" for ACCOUNTING purposes.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Corporation Tax, Inhabitant Tax, and Enterprise Tax</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Three distinct taxes, together forming Japan's "income tax" accounting concept</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-1-2">
            <span>Tax</span>
            <span>Description</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-2"><span>Corporation tax (法人税)</span><span>The primary NATIONAL tax on corporate taxable income</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-1-2"><span>Inhabitant tax (住民税)</span><span>LOCAL (prefectural/municipal) tax, generally calculated with reference to corporation tax liability and a per-capita component</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-1-2"><span>Enterprise tax (事業税)</span><span>LOCAL (prefectural) tax, with BOTH an income-based component AND, for larger companies, a size-based ("pro forma standard") component (Section 4)</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>THE KEY NUANCE — the Size-Based Portion of Enterprise Tax</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A genuinely distinctive Japan-specific classification question</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">For LARGER companies, enterprise tax includes a "PRO FORMA STANDARD TAXATION" (外形標準課税) component — calculated based on FACTORS such as VALUE ADDED and CAPITAL, RATHER than purely on taxable INCOME. This raises a genuinely DISTINCTIVE classification question: since this portion is NOT fundamentally based on the entity's INCOME, is it truly an "income tax" for accounting purposes? Under J-GAAP practice, the INCOME-BASED portion of enterprise tax IS treated as CURRENT TAX EXPENSE (within the "Corporation, Inhabitant, and Enterprise Taxes" line), while the SIZE-BASED (pro forma standard) portion is generally treated as an ORDINARY OPERATING EXPENSE (within SG&amp;A) INSTEAD — a NUANCED classification distinction WITHOUT a close IFRS or US GAAP parallel, since NEITHER framework has an EQUIVALENT tax construct of this SPECIFIC type.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Recognition Timing for Current Tax Expense</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Recognised in the period the related taxable income arises</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">CURRENT tax expense is recognised in the SAME period as the TAXABLE income (or loss) it relates to — with a CORRESPONDING current tax LIABILITY (or receivable, for tax refunds due) recognised on the Balance Sheet, REGARDLESS of when the actual tax PAYMENT is due.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Worked Example — Classifying Enterprise Tax Between Income-Based and Size-Based Portions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Splitting the tax charge by nature</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A large company's enterprise tax liability</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A large company's total enterprise tax for the year is ¥45,000,000, comprising ¥30,000,000 based on taxable income and ¥15,000,000 based on the pro forma standard (value added and capital) factors.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The ¥30,000,000 INCOME-BASED portion is classified as <strong>CURRENT TAX EXPENSE</strong> (within the income tax line). The ¥15,000,000 SIZE-BASED portion is classified as an <strong>OPERATING EXPENSE</strong> WITHIN SG&amp;A — NOT as part of income tax expense — reflecting that it is NOT fundamentally based on the company's income.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — Total Current Tax Expense</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Combining all three layered taxes</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Combining corporation, inhabitant, and income-based enterprise tax</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company's corporation tax is ¥200,000,000, inhabitant tax is ¥25,000,000, and the income-based portion of enterprise tax is ¥30,000,000.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">TOTAL CURRENT TAX EXPENSE = ¥200,000,000 + ¥25,000,000 + ¥30,000,000 = <strong>¥255,000,000</strong> — presented TOGETHER as a SINGLE "Corporation, Inhabitant, and Enterprise Taxes" line in the Statement of Income.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 27 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Current tax expense recognised, and its components across the layered tax system</span>
          <span>Basis for classifying the size-based enterprise tax portion as an operating expense</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Correctly splitting enterprise tax between its income-based and size-based components</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Estimated current tax liability where the final tax return has not yet been filed</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">A genuinely distinctive Japan-specific tax structure</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">IAS 12 and ASC 740 BOTH address "income taxes" as taxes based SUBSTANTIALLY on TAXABLE profit — NEITHER framework has an EQUIVALENT concept to Japan's LAYERED national/local tax system, OR the SPECIFIC classification question raised by a SIZE-BASED (non-income) enterprise tax component. This makes ASBJ Statement No. 27's Section 4 classification NUANCE a GENUINELY DISTINCTIVE, Japan-SPECIFIC feature, rather than a divergence from a SPECIFIC IFRS/US GAAP treatment of the SAME underlying transaction type.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every current tax event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Income-based current tax</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Presented as income tax expense</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Size-based enterprise tax</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Presented as an operating expense, not income tax</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 28</span><span>Tax Effect Accounting — supplies the DEFERRED tax counterpart to this Statement's CURRENT tax treatment</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Pro forma standard taxation (外形標準課税)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The size-based component of enterprise tax applicable to larger companies, calculated based on value added and capital rather than income.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">Enterprise tax (事業税)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A local prefectural tax comprising an income-based component (treated as income tax expense) and, for larger companies, a size-based component (treated as an operating expense).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
        <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
        <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
        <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
        <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer-note">ASBJ Statement No. 27 — Accounting Standard for Current Income Taxes · Extended Reference Poster · Self-contained, no internet connection required</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
